---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const url = 'https://shitster.org';
const campaignUrl = 'https://dashoff.org';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/mrbese/shitster';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="shitster · Omer Bese"
  description="shitster: consumer self-help campaigns. The tool prepares, the human acts."
  path="/shitster"
>
  <div class="phead reveal">
    <div class="eyebrow">shitster</div>
    <h1>Consumer self-help campaigns. The tool prepares, the human acts<span class="d">.</span></h1>
  </div>

  <section class="body">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        BMW pushed a Spider-Man ad to the dashboard of cars people own, on a screen it once
        called a private space. I read the 28-page contract they wrote, found the clause where
        they obligate themselves to call every complaining owner back individually, and built
        the tool that generates those letters in the browser. Zero accounts, zero stored data,
        open source. First campaign: DashOff. Every big brand should carry a shitster budget.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="links ctas">
      <a href={url}>shitster.org <span class="ar">&#8599;</span></a>
      <a href={campaignUrl}>dashoff.org <span class="ar">&#8599;</span></a>
      <a href={repoUrl}>github.com/mrbese/shitster <span class="ar">&#8599;</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .body{margin-top:56px}
  .body .prose{max-width:var(--measure)}
  .ctas{margin-top:28px}
</style>
